From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: bridge: tc358764: initialize Matisse PPI before BTA reads

The exact Samsung r01 bridge sequence begins with generic LP writes to
configure PPI, enable lanes and start DSI, without a preceding DSI ID read.
On the physical SM-T531, ID0x6500 is verified over its independent I2C
interface before native takeover. The current upstream-style BTA ID read
instead returns zero data and prevents every configuration write.

Follow the verified write-first sequence for the Matisse profile only.
All configuration writes retain transfer-length/error checks. Other boards
keep their ID read. This is a board bring-up experiment, not proof that BTA
is unsupported: validate configuration readback and actual LCD output.

Source: LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226 commit
3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256,
arch/arm/boot/dts/msm8226/dsi_panel_tc358764_wxga_video-r01.dtsi.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/tc358764.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/tc358764.c
index e8163b6c2..db6ae64e2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/tc358764.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/tc358764.c
@@ -218,10 +218,13 @@ static int tc358764_init(struct tc358764 *ctx)
 {
 	u32 v = 0;
 
-	tc358764_read(ctx, SYS_ID, &v);
-	if (ctx->error)
-		return tc358764_clear_error(ctx);
-	dev_info(ctx->dev, "ID: %#x\n", v);
+	/* Samsung brings up the PPI with writes before any BTA read. */
+	if (!ctx->matisse) {
+		tc358764_read(ctx, SYS_ID, &v);
+		if (ctx->error)
+			return tc358764_clear_error(ctx);
+		dev_info(ctx->dev, "ID: %#x\n", v);
+	}
 
 	/* configure PPI counters */
 	tc358764_write(ctx, PPI_TX_RX_TA, ctx->matisse ? 0x50006 : TTA_GET | TTA_SURE);
